{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "API contract context for the PipelineGuard fix agent.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. PR #130 was an agent fix that mis-diagnosed its own",
    "finding: it guarded ciiImpact when the crash was formatFuel(voyage.actualFuel)",
    "throwing on an undefined, because /voyage/history was sending actual_fuel.",
    "Replaying that selection (see d4-demo/BASELINE.md) showed the model HAD both",
    "sides of the boundary and still fixed the wrong field. What it lacked was the",
    "declared type and the formatter signature -- the two things that turn an odd",
    "key into a contract violation. Text-similarity ranking cannot find those:",
    "they scored 6, under six irrelevant same-directory siblings. So we declare",
    "them.",
    "",
    "AUTHORING RULES:",
    "  - anchor must match EXACTLY ONE line in the file. An ambiguous anchor is",
    "    refused and the whole file is shown instead (manifest_ambiguous).",
    "  - a missing anchor is refused the same way (manifest_stale). Both surface",
    "    as errors on the fix run, so a drifted manifest is loud, not silent.",
    "  - editable: true means 'the fix may land here'. Everything else is",
    "    reference the model may read and may NOT patch.",
    "  - keep each feature under 6 read-only entries and 24KB.",
    "  - a terms-only feature (no page_prefix) must use DISTINCTIVE terms.",
    "    Scoring is +1 per matched term, so a feature listing common words wins",
    "    over one listing few specific ones. 'fleet' and 'vessel' are in every",
    "    finding in a fleet-management app: an early draft of the 'fleet' feature",
    "    used them and stole an ETS compliance finding from 'compliance'.",
    "    Prefer multi-word phrases that only that feature's findings would say.",
    "",
    "Verify after editing, free and with no model call:",
    "  python agents/fix/harness.py --findings <f.json> --repo . --dry-run",
    "and check the run reports no manifest_ warnings."
  ],
